From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: diamondStar35 <ramymaherali55@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:54:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/sofalizer: update direction without reloading SOFA data

Retain the dataset, lookup tables, FFT plans, and input history for runtime
rotation and elevation commands. Prepare responses in a spare bank and
crossfade outputs over 10 ms, coalescing pending requests. Use overlap-save
in frequency mode so input history remains valid when coefficients change.

Use floating-point spherical coordinates without applying modulo 90 to
latitude, preserving both poles and fractional angles.
---
diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 37f9123df497ee28b106ffbc32f959ee590ce057..4a1a83b93f797a207c6c7636174e89ce3fd3c63a 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -6762,6 +6762,18 @@ Set neighbor search angle step. Only used if option @var{interpolate} is enabled
 Set neighbor search radius step. Only used if option @var{interpolate} is enabled.
 @end table
 
+@subsection Commands
+
+This filter supports the @command{rotation} and @command{elevation} commands,
+using the same ranges as the corresponding options. Elevation values of
+@code{-90} and @code{90} select the poles without wrapping to zero.
+
+Direction commands reuse the loaded SOFA data and processing buffers. New
+responses take effect at an audio frame boundary and crossfade over 10 milliseconds.
+If a transition is still running, the most recent pending direction is applied
+after it finishes. The @option{interpolate} option controls interpolation between
+measured directions independently of this transition.
+
 @subsection Examples
 
 @itemize
